      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}\n\nsorry this took soo long. I was, and still am, getting over something.\n\nA method to sync local animation chains was actually easily known despite a good number of people not knowing it, any parameter in animation chains for contacts, sounds, etc. would also exist in the expression parameters in the avatar descriptor which would be set to synced. contacts simply had to be set to local and use this trick, this synced sounds, grabbable props, and contacts that could trigger specific sounds across the network. and I learnt of this trick through a basic tutorial that was made for the vrchat community to help explain the 3.0 sdk.\n\nHowever, I cannot explain it, but it seems that this simple method no longer functioned after the 2022 migration and wound up making avatars look rather janky when looking away mid animation.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
